From 6e63273bfb1c644a08cbf05a1cebc197b42f334e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:10:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] B70-0041: hot/cold route counter (B70_MOE_ROUTE_COUNT):
 cold share of routed experts, per layer counts as JSON

Each hot/cold layer adds its topk_ids to a per-layer device counter (works inside FULL graph replays,
where no Python runs). The runner reads the counters on the host right after the per-step sync it already
does for the NVMe PLE path, every B70_MOE_ROUTE_COUNT_S seconds (default 60), logs the share of this
rank's routes that went to cold (pinned host) experts and writes the cumulative counts to
B70_MOE_ROUTE_COUNT_PATH-rank<r>.json. Off by default; with it off nothing changes.

Port to 0.32 (from Niluthon/qwen38-flash-tp2@e536e33, Apache-2.0, via our 0.30 carry): the per-period host read (maybe_dump_routes) moves to the top of Qwen4ExpModelState.prepare_inputs; 0.32 has no NVMe-PLE host sync at the old place, so the read syncs once per B70_MOE_ROUTE_COUNT_S period.
